From 5796daf6be5ef18f07ca56b98c0a6215d8ae0b29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 02:36:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0222 -- SDL_HINT_DOS_MOUSE_LEVEL_ONLY: switch
 0221's press delivery off at run time

WHY: with 0221 in every build, a check that lost clicks stay at 0 (dosags
tests/ratchet.yaml lost-inputs) can no longer be shown to fail: the quick
clicks that used to be lost now arrive. A check whose control cannot make
it fail proves nothing (the ratchet reports it NOPOWER). The control needs
the pre-0221 behaviour in the same binary, not an old binary that the
nightly build cannot reproduce. The same switch is the field fallback if
0221's delivery ever misbehaves with some mouse driver.

WHAT: SDL_HINT_DOS_MOUSE_LEVEL_ONLY=1 (environment, read once) makes the
pump use the level read alone, as before 0221. 0220's counters stay:
function 5 is still read every pump into hw, seen counts level edges only,
so lost = hw - seen shows what the level read missed. Unset (the default),
0221 runs unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nz9XeKeVG8Ab7dm8esJsMu
---
 src/video/dos/SDL_dosevents.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/video/dos/SDL_dosevents.c b/src/video/dos/SDL_dosevents.c
index fe49c401e..e6b75c611 100644
--- a/src/video/dos/SDL_dosevents.c
+++ b/src/video/dos/SDL_dosevents.c
@@ -512,6 +512,24 @@ void DOSVESA_PumpEvents(SDL_VideoDevice *device)
            presses DELIVERED (level edges + these), so 0220's lost = hw -
            seen reads 0 when nothing is missed, and a negative value would
            be a phantom press. Position: the current one. */
+        /* dosags patch 0222: SDL_HINT_DOS_MOUSE_LEVEL_ONLY=1 turns 0221's
+           delivery off (read once): the level read alone, as before 0221,
+           with 0220's counters still kept (read every pump, seen = level
+           edges only), so lost = hw - seen shows what the level read missed.
+           For controls that must prove a lost-click check can fail, and as a
+           field fallback. */
+        static int level_only = -1;
+        if (level_only < 0) {
+            const char *e = SDL_getenv("SDL_HINT_DOS_MOUSE_LEVEL_ONLY");
+            level_only = (e && e[0] == '1' && e[1] == 0) ? 1 : 0;
+        }
+        if (level_only) {
+            const Uint16 down_edges = (Uint16)(buttons & ~dos_mouse_prev_buttons);
+            DOS_ReadMousePressCounters();
+            dos_mouse_new_presses[0] = dos_mouse_new_presses[1] = 0;
+            dos_mouse_seen_presses += (Uint32)(((down_edges >> 0) & 1) + ((down_edges >> 1) & 1));
+            dos_mouse_prev_buttons = buttons;
+        } else
         {
             static const Uint8 sdl_button[2] = { SDL_BUTTON_LEFT, SDL_BUTTON_RIGHT };
             int b;
-- 
